# ============================================================================
# FEE3411 Publication/ — this is the git repo, and the site it builds is
# PUBLIC. Git history is permanent, so what is excluded here matters.
# ============================================================================

# ---- src/ is NOT committed -------------------------------------------------
# src/ (the copy of the LaTeX sources ./sync.sh pulls in) stays local only.
# It carries full solution / marking-scheme text in the clear -- the STRIP
# step in web/build_site.sh only redacts a scratch copy under build/, never
# src/ itself -- so it must never reach the public repo. Only the *generated*
# docs/ (Markdown + SVG, already redacted) is committed; see docs/ below.
#
# Build locally before pushing:  ./sync.sh && web/build_site.sh
src/

# ---- NEVER COMMIT ---------------------------------------------------------
# Backstops in case something is ever placed here by hand, since src/ above
# already keeps these out in the normal flow.
#   Books/       the four copyrighted set texts
#   Attendance/  student personal data
#   *marking-scheme*, *-solutions.pdf -- see the src/ note above
Books/
Attendance/
*Attendance*.xlsx
*marking-scheme*
*-solutions.pdf

# Internal planning documents.
FEE3411_Course_Spec.md
Claude outputs/
NOTES.md

# ---- generated by web/build_site.sh, but NOT ignored -----------------------
# docs/notes/, docs/tutorials/, docs/assignments/, docs/supplementary/ and
# docs/pdf/ ARE committed -- they're the whole point of this repo now that
# src/ isn't here. docs/index.md, docs/tutorials.md, docs/assignments.md,
# docs/resources.md etc. are hand-written landing pages and were always
# committed. Only true scratch output stays ignored:
build/
site_build/

# ---- LaTeX build artefacts (produced by build/ during a local build) ------
*.aux
*.log
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.tmp
tmp*.tmp

# ---- misc -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
